@startuml
' Figure 7.2  Where the key is minted
' Reading order: top to bottom. The control plane mints the key with
' the permission, before the first attempt. The executor reserves it in
' the ledger and sends the same key on every attempt.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
participant "Agent loop" as A <<model>>
participant "Control plane" as C <<policy>>
participant "Executor" as X <<ops>>
database "Effect ledger" as L <<evidence>>
participant "Processor" as N <<ops>>
A -> C : proposal
C -[$POLICY]-> X : permission + key
X -> L : reserve(key)
X -> N : refund(key)
N -[$FAIL]-> X : timeout
X -> L : unknown
X -> N : refund(key)
N --> X : stored receipt
X -[$VERIFIED]-> L : committed
note over X : never mint a key\ninside the retry loop
@enduml
